I'm now revising `addTransaction` within `App.tsx` and the `Transaction` interface in `types.ts` to accommodate UUIDs. I'll ensure the `user_id` is passed correctly when creating transactions. My current thinking is to make the `Transaction` interface accept a string for `user_id` while maintaining the SQL UUID type. This approach will allow us to migrate. I'm updating `dbService.ts` to expect UUIDs for data integrity, making sure the code is resilient. I will be sure the user can be identified, even if no UUID is passed.


