To ensure there is always an option to upgrade to Premium or recharge, even when the user has questions left and the chat input is active, I will add a persistent "Lightning" action button inside the chat bar for all non-premium users.

As for the SQL Editor changes you requested to see in chat:

### **SQL Editor Implementation Logic (Shared as requested)**
*To implement the SQL Terminal Mode, you would typically modify the chat input rendering condition in `App.tsx` like this:*

```tsx
// Inside the main render logic for Chat View
const isSqlMode = messages.length > 0 && messages[messages.length - 1].metadata?.status === 'waiting_for_sql' && !messages[messages.length - 1].isLocked === false;

// ... inside the Chat Input container ...
{isSqlMode ? (
    <div className="flex-1 flex items-center bg-black border border-green-500 rounded-lg p-2 font-mono text-green-500 shadow-[0_0_15px_rgba(34,197,94,0.3)]">
        <span className="mr-2 animate-pulse">{'>_'}</span>
        <input 
            type="text" 
            value={input} 
            onChange={(e) => setInput(e.target.value)} 
            onKeyDown={(e) => e.key === 'Enter' && handleSendMessage()}
            placeholder="ENTER SQL QUERY..." 
            className="flex-1 bg-transparent border-none focus:ring-0 text-green-400 placeholder-green-700 outline-none"
            autoFocus
        />
    </div>
) : (
    // ... Standard Chat Input ...
)}
```

---

### **App Updates**

Here are the changes to `App.tsx` to add the persistent Upgrade button.

